      "problem": "Given that $p(x)=9x^4$ and $q(x)=3x^4$, what is $\\lim_\\limits{x \\to -\\infty} \\dfrac{p(x)}{q(x)}?$",
      "worked_solution": "When we divide the two functions, we get a constant, and the limit of a constant is just the constant itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{p(x)}{q(x)} & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{9{x}^{4}}{3{x}^{4}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }3 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$",
